Setting an array length to five million.
-- script.js --
const a = [];
try { a.length = 5000000; return a.length; } catch (e) { return [e.name, e.message]; }
-- tools.json --
{}
-- divergence --
Huge sparse lengths are stored lazily by Goja; the engine raises ErrRuntimeUnsupported past 65536 holes instead of materializing them (hosts fall back before any effect).
